CODE
This product is based on Word Atlas (词光) — https://github.com/designfuchen/word-atlas
Copyright (c) 2026 Word Atlas contributors, licensed under the MIT License (see LICENSE).
Reused and adapted from Word Atlas: project structure (React + Vite + hash router),
the localStorage store and backup format, the FSRS scheduling wrapper (src/store/srs.ts),
the session/queue logic (src/store/session.ts), the Sheet/Toast UI primitives, the
celebration burst (src/lib/burst.ts), the service worker media cache and the offline download.

CONTENT — Word Atlas contributors — CC BY 4.0
Files under public/wa/ (illustrations, UK/US pronunciation recordings, example sentences,
collocations, word families, synonyms/antonyms, tips) and data/word-atlas-manifest.json come
from Word Atlas, upstream commit 19a9bd88:
  Word Atlas contributors — CC BY 4.0 — https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
Modifications by 小词芽: only the 1,399 entries matching 小词芽's grade 1–6 word list were kept;
images re-used as 256px WebP thumbnails; example-sentence audio was not copied; examples and
collocations were re-filtered by grade (a "core" kid tier and a separate "ext"/进阶 tier);
content unsuitable for children (violence, adult themes, substances, crime) was removed;
44 entries whose upstream sense differs from the school meaning (e.g. bear = 忍受) keep no
picture and only advanced content. Produced by scripts/import_word_atlas.py.
These modifications are not endorsed by the Word Atlas contributors.

WORD LIST (data/wordlist-v2.csv, see data/ATTRIBUTION.md)
- CEFR-J Wordlist Version 1.5. 『CEFR-J Wordlist Version 1.5』 東京外国語大学投野由紀夫研究室.
  http://www.cefr-j.org/download.html
- NGSL 1.2 (Browne, Culligan & Phillips 2013) and FrequencyWords (Hermit Dave, OpenSubtitles 2018),
  CC BY-SA 4.0 — used only for the ngsl_rank / freq_rank_subtitles columns of the CSV in data/.
  Those columns are redistributed in this repository under CC BY-SA 4.0 with this attribution;
  they are NOT bundled into the app (src/data/lexicon-v2.json ships only en/zh/pos/grade/topic/picture).
- ECDICT (skywind3000), MIT — Chinese glosses where zh_source=ECDICT(MIT).
- Dolch sight words — public domain.
- Cambridge YLE wordlists (© UCLES 2018), 《义务教育英语课程标准（2022年版）》 and 人教版 PEP 词表
  were used as grade-level signals only; their lists are not reproduced.

Third-party:
- ts-fsrs (MIT) — spaced-repetition scheduler.
- lucide-react (ISC) — icons.
- Emoji artwork: rendered by the device's emoji font.
- Pronunciation fallback when no Word Atlas recording exists: the device's speech synthesis
  voice, then online TTS (Youdao dictvoice, then Google Translate TTS) streamed at play time.
